#
# WHAT IT ADDS: --alpha_proj_source sham — a RANK-MATCHED RANDOM projector. It fits the
# real holdout projector first (identical code path, so the removed rank r is whatever the
# honest cell would have used), then discards it and builds P = I − Q Qᵀ from a random
# orthonormal basis Q of that SAME rank r. Everything downstream (the edit loop, the value
# optimisation, the full forward pass, the damage measurement) is byte-identical to the
# holdout cell; the ONLY difference is which subspace is removed.
#
# THE TEST THIS ENABLES: within-probe rho(key-cos, damage-removed) under sham vs under the
# real holdout projector, same layer/seed. If the geometry-tracking is an algebraic
# consequence of "projecting something out", sham reproduces it. If it comes from removing
# the PRESERVED-KEY subspace specifically, sham does not. This is the objection the
# withdrawn CPU proxy could not address (see
# submissions/ieee/revision/SHAM-CONTROL-READOUT-20260726.md).
#
# PROVENANCE: alpha_proj_source is already recorded into the npz/json (killgate lines
# ~787/820/897/988/1010), so "sham" self-labels in every artifact; proj_disjoint stays 1
# because sham != probes. Cells write to their own tags (g4_*_alphaSHAM_*), never colliding
# with holdout artifacts.
